  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed), but I didn't add a test for this case.\n\nThe bug was in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`. A child context inherited its parent's whole `default_map`, so a subcommand looked for its options in the top-level dict instead of its own entry. It now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which is the nested `{'runserver': {'port': 5000}}` form that `docs/commands.md` describes.\n\nIf the parent map has no entry for the subcommand, `.get()` returns `None`, so that subcommand gets no `default_map` and any `default_map` entries for its own subcommands are dropped.",
